Tired of sending the same four operators on every mission? With [b]Off Duty[/b], operators [b]get tired from back-to-back deployments[/b] and [b]recover while they're off duty[/b], so the rest of your company gets a chance to shine.
[b]Off Duty is in development.[/b] This page describes the planned first release; details and numbers will change with playtesting.

[heading]Features[/heading]
[list]
[*][b]Fatigue from deployment, not damage[/b]: every mission an operator goes on wears them down. Long missions and going down add more. Even a flawless squad needs a rest eventually.[/*]
[*][b]Rest brings them back[/b]: each cycle an operator sits out, they recover.[/*]
[*][b]Your call, always[/b]: a Tired operator takes a small penalty next mission. An Exhausted one takes a bigger penalty, and pushing them anyway means a longer recovery afterwards. You're never locked out of deploying anyone.[/*]
[*][b]Story-safe[/b]: operators the story needs can always deploy, so no campaign can get stuck.[/*]
[*][b]No surprises[/b]: squad select shows the exact penalty, and what pushing will cost, before you commit.[/*]
[*][b]Separate from injuries[/b]: the game's own injuries work exactly as before.[/*]
[/list]

[heading]Requirements[/heading]
[list]
[*][b]Star Wars Zero Company[/b][/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarszerocompany/mods/9]UE4SS for Star Wars Zero Company[/url][/*]
[/list]

[heading]Installation[/heading]
[b]Mod manager[/b]
Off Duty includes metadata for the community mod managers:
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarszerocompany/mods/29]ZCOM Mod Manager[/url][/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarszerocompany/mods/121]Zero Company Mod Command[/url][/*]
[/list]
Install the downloaded ZIP through either one and make sure Off Duty is enabled.

[b]Manual installation[/b]
Make sure UE4SS is installed and working, close the game, then extract the [b]OffDuty[/b] folder into:
[code]SWZeroCompany/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/Mods/[/code]
The finished installation should contain:
[code]ue4ss/Mods/OffDuty/Scripts/main.lua[/code]
The package includes [b]enabled.txt[/b]. If your UE4SS setup doesn't pick it up, add this line to [b]ue4ss/Mods/mods.txt[/b]:
[code]OffDuty : 1[/code]
[b]Updating:[/b] close the game first, then install the new ZIP the same way (by hand, copy the new [b]OffDuty[/b] folder over the old one).

[b]Uninstalling[/b]
Switch Off Duty off or remove it in your mod manager, or delete the [b]OffDuty[/b] folder.

[heading]Known Issues[/heading]
[list]
[*]Restart the game after installing or updating Off Duty. Don't use UE4SS's "Reload All Mods"; it can crash or freeze the game.[/*]
[/list]

[heading]Troubleshooting[/heading]
Off Duty writes diagnostic information to [b]off_duty.log[/b] in its [b]OffDuty[/b] folder. [b]UE4SS.log[/b] remains the primary startup and crash log.
When reporting a problem, please include:
[list]
[*]Your game build[/*]
[*]Your UE4SS version[/*]
[*]Your other installed mods[/*]
[*]What you were doing and what happened[/*]
[*][code]UE4SS.log[/code] and [code]off_duty.log[/code][/*]
[/list]
The logs only contain technical details about what the mod did: no screenshots, saves or personal files. They may mention folder paths on your PC, so feel free to look them over before sending.

[heading]Source Code and Issue Reports[/heading]
Source, technical documentation and issue tracking are available on [url=https://github.com/chatterchats/ZComOffDuty]GitHub[/url]. You can also post in the Bugs tab here on Nexus.

